<title>BELGIUM: Belgium to reach 2.9% 1997 deficit target - minister.</title>
<headline>Belgium to reach 2.9% 1997 deficit target - minister.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgium will reach the government's 1997 budget deficit target of 2.9 percent of Gross Domestic Product, budget minister Herman Van Rompuy said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;For 1997 we have every hope - even the certainty - that we will reach the 2.9 percent target,&quot; Van Rompuy told a news conference.  </p>
<p>Earlier the budget and finance ministries said Belgium's 1996 budget deficit was 3.4 percent of GDP, overshooting the government's forecast of 3.2 percent.</p>
